I tend to carry all items (except rocks) that I find on a level to a
local stash near the down stairs.  That includes gold.

When I finish exploring a level I tend to shuttle up to pick out the
best items for my stash as I gradually explore deeper.  Or in the case
of the mines below mine town I shuttle them up towards the main dungeon.
As such in the early game my main stash is near the stairs one level up
from me.

At some point later in the game I tend to build my main stash as a base
camp on a level with an altar.  By then I may well have lost interest in
gold and the gold ends up in one of my level stashes.


